{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Braiding.HeckeGenPolyReduction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Braiding.HeckeGenPolyReduction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.Algebra","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Module"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.hecke_gen_poly_reduction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.hecke_gen_poly_reduction","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/HeckeGenPolyReduction.lean#L67-L87","doc":"**Single-generator Hecke polynomial reduction** (Cayley–Hamilton).\n\nFor `σ : A` satisfying the Hecke quadratic `σ * σ = h • σ + 1`, every\nproduct `∏ⱼ (σ + dⱼ • 1)` equals `α • σ + β • 1` with `(α, β) = heckeAB h ds`.\nProof: induction on `ds`, using only the quadratic relation (no division).\n\nThis makes the per-generator block of the transfer-matrix χ a single\n`α·D(δ′) + β` evaluation; see the module docstring. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:hecke-generator-poly-reduction","label":"prop:hecke-generator-poly-reduction","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-generator-poly-reduction.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.heckeAB_cons_snd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.heckeAB_cons_snd","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/HeckeGenPolyReduction.lean#L64-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.heckeAB_cons_fst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.heckeAB_cons_fst","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/HeckeGenPolyReduction.lean#L61-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.heckeAB_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.heckeAB_cons","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/HeckeGenPolyReduction.lean#L56-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.heckeAB_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.heckeAB_nil","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/HeckeGenPolyReduction.lean#L54-L54","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.heckeAB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.heckeAB","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/HeckeGenPolyReduction.lean#L45-L52","doc":"Division-free reduction coefficients `(α, β)` for `∏ⱼ (σ + dⱼ•1)`,\ndriven by the Hecke quadratic `σ*σ = h•σ + 1` with `h = q − q⁻¹`.\nEmpty list ↦ `(0, 1)` (the empty product is `1 = 0•σ + 1•1`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}